  "audience": "family",
  "keyIdea": "A solid keeps its shape, a liquid flows and takes the shape of its container, and a gas spreads out to fill any space.",
  "explain": {
    "kid": [
      "A block of ice is a solid. It keeps its shape.",
      "Water is a liquid. It runs and fills the bottom of a cup. Air is a gas. It spreads out to fill the room."
    ],
    "adult": [
      "Solids are hard and keep their shape. Liquids are runny: they flow, pour and take the shape of the container. Gases spread out to fill the space, and you often cannot see them.",
      "Tricky cases help. Sand pours, but each grain is a solid. Honey is a slow liquid. Steam is water as a gas."
    ]
  },
